  "worked_solution": "Looking at the matrix $T$, we can see that $T$ represents a horizontal shear of shear factor $-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore, the image of the square $R$ under $T$ is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/4b6cfc485ffa74f141e3dc4b8fad61b48103808a4f4c29b2dc5180f634902c4f.png)\n\n**Alternative method:**\n\nWe can check that the vertices of $R$ are mapped to the vertices of the parallelogram shown above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
